window.AeroMilData=[
{id:`m01`,date:`2025-09-17`,service:`USA`,aircraft:`MH-60`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Near Summit Lake, west of Olympia, Washington`,lat:47.05,lon:-123.1,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`night`,`lowlevel`],phase:`low level`,fatal:true,narrative:`A 160th Special Operations Aviation Regiment MH 60 Black Hawk crashed at night during a training mission near Summit Lake in Thurston County, west of Olympia, Washington. All four soldiers aboard were killed.`,hazard:`Night low altitude training over forested ridges calls for a current wire and obstacle check for the planned route and any deviation from it.`,source_title:`Helicopter crash near Joint Base Lewis McChord (Stars and Stripes)`,source_url:`https://www.stripes.com/theaters/us/2025-09-18/helicopter-crash-joint-base-lewis-mcchord-19134367.html`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m02`,date:`2025-01-29`,service:`USA`,aircraft:`UH-60L`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Potomac River near Reagan National Airport, Washington, D.C.`,lat:38.846,lon:-77.035,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`midair`,`civil_conflict`,`night`,`lowlevel`,`water`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`An Army UH 60L flying a published helicopter route along the Potomac at night collided with a regional jet on approach to Reagan National, killing all 67 people aboard both aircraft. The NTSB found the route was placed too close to a runway approach path, the air traffic system relied too heavily on visual separation, and the helicopter crew did not apply effective visual separation. The board also found the Army had not made sure its pilots understood barometric altimeter error tolerances, which bore on the helicopter flying above the route's altitude limit.`,hazard:`In busy terminal airspace at night, do not rely on visual separation alone, cross check altimeter tolerances against route altitude limits, and positively identify the specific traffic called by ATC.`,source_title:`NTSB investigation DCA25MA108, mid air collision near Ronald Reagan Washington National Airport`,source_url:`https://www.ntsb.gov/investigations/Pages/DCA25MA108.aspx`,source_kind:`NTSB`},
{id:`m03`,date:`2025-01-28`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`F-35A`,family:`fighter`,place:`Eielson AFB, Alaska`,lat:64.665,lon:-147.1,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`mx`],phase:`approach`,fatal:!1,narrative:`After takeoff from Eielson in extreme cold, an F 35A's nose landing gear would not retract properly because water contaminated hydraulic fluid had frozen in the strut. During attempts to fix it, ice in the main gear struts caused the jet's sensors to read that it was on the ground, the flight controls shifted to ground mode while airborne, and the aircraft became uncontrollable. The pilot ejected with minor injuries and the jet was destroyed.`,hazard:`In extreme cold, a landing gear malfunction can cascade into flight control problems, so plan fuel, divert options, and controllability checks before attempting repeated gear troubleshooting.`,source_title:`Press Release: Aircraft Accident Investigation Report Released for Eielson F-35 Crash`,source_url:`https://www.eielson.af.mil/News/Display/Article/4286209/`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m04`,date:`2024-10-15`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`EA-18G`,family:`attack`,place:`East of Mount Rainier, Cascade Range, Washington`,lat:46.85,lon:-121.55,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`cfit`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`An EA 18G Growler from NAS Whidbey Island crashed on a mountainside east of Mount Rainier during a routine training flight. Both crew members were killed. The wreckage was found at about 6,000 feet in remote, steep, snow covered and heavily wooded terrain.`,hazard:`Training in the Cascades puts high terrain close to flight paths, so brief minimum safe altitudes and terrain clearance for the route and the weather.`,source_title:`Growler crew dies in crash near Rainier`,source_url:`https://www.laconnerweeklynews.com/story/2024/10/23/news/growler-crew-dies-in-crash-near-rainier/11117.html`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m05`,date:`2024-03-08`,service:`ARNG`,aircraft:`UH-72`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`La Grulla, near Rio Grande City, Texas`,lat:26.27,lon:-98.65,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`lowlevel`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A National Guard UH 72 Lakota supporting the federal border security mission crashed near Rio Grande City in Starr County during an afternoon flight. Two National Guard soldiers and a Border Patrol agent were killed, and a third soldier aboard was critically injured.`,hazard:`Border surveillance flying often means long periods at low altitude near the river, so brief obstacle awareness and power margins for the mission profile.`,source_title:`Helicopter carrying National Guardsmen and Border Patrol agent crashes in Texas, killing 3`,source_url:`https://www.nbcsandiego.com/news/national-international/helicopter-crashes-along-us-mexico-border-texas-authorities-say/3456956/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m06`,date:`2024-02-23`,service:`ARNG`,aircraft:`AH-64D`,family:`helo_attack`,place:`Near Booneville, Prentiss County, Mississippi`,lat:34.66,lon:-88.57,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Mississippi Army National Guard AH 64D Apache crashed into a wooded area near Booneville in Prentiss County around 2 p.m. during a routine training flight. Both pilots, who served at the Guard's aviation support facility in Tupelo, were killed.`,hazard:`Even routine local training warrants a full brief of emergency procedures and suitable forced landing areas over wooded terrain.`,source_title:`Mississippi National Guard update on helicopter crash`,source_url:`https://www.ng.ms.gov/sites/msng/files/news/attachments/2024-02/PRESS%20RELEASE%202024-0224-002%20MSNG%20Update%20on%20Helicopter%20Crash.pdf`,source_kind:`press release`},
{id:`m07`,date:`2024-02-06`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`CH-53E`,family:`helo_heavy`,place:`Mountain ridge near Pine Valley, California`,lat:32.82,lon:-116.53,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`cfit`,`nvg`,`wx`,`night`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A CH 53E returning to MCAS Miramar overnight struck a mountain ridge near Pine Valley, killing five Marines. The investigation found the pilot failed to avoid terrain and keep visual flight visibility and clearance, with low clouds and icing hiding the mountains and precipitation likely degrading the crew's night vision goggles. It also found the squadron commander should not have approved the flight.`,hazard:`Set firm weather and terrain clearance limits for night goggle flights over mountains, and plan an instrument or alternate route when clouds and precipitation hide the ridges.`,source_title:`Weather, night vision goggles were likely factors in Marine Corps helicopter crash, report finds`,source_url:`https://www.bostonglobe.com/2025/05/07/nation/weather-night-vision-goggles-were-likely-factors-marine-corps-helicopter-crash-report-finds`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m08`,date:`2024-01-04`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`B-1B`,family:`bomber`,place:`Ellsworth AFB, South Dakota`,lat:44.145,lon:-103.1,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`wx`],phase:`landing`,fatal:!1,narrative:`Two B 1Bs returned from a training sortie and flew low visibility approaches to Ellsworth in low clouds and fog with shifting winds. The crew of the second bomber did not manage airspeed and approach angle, the aircraft hit the ground short of the runway and was destroyed by fire, and all four crew ejected with two treated for injuries. The board cited poor crew coordination, weather, ineffective supervision, limited awareness of airfield conditions, and a unit culture that tolerated declining airmanship.`,hazard:`On a low visibility approach in shear, watch the power setting after a gust driven speed increase and have the other pilot call speed and glidepath deviations out loud.`,source_title:`B-1B Ellsworth Accident Investigation Board report released (AFGSC)`,source_url:`https://www.afgsc.af.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/3850845/`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m09`,date:`2023-11-20`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`P-8A`,family:`patrol`,place:`Marine Corps Air Station Kaneohe Bay, Oahu, Hawaii`,lat:21.45,lon:-157.77,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`water`],phase:`landing`,fatal:!1,narrative:`A Navy P 8A on detachment for maritime homeland defense overran the runway while landing at MCAS Kaneohe Bay and came to rest in shallow water about 50 yards offshore. All nine people aboard evacuated safely with no immediate injuries reported.`,hazard:`Runways that end at the water leave no overrun margin, so brief landing distance, touchdown point and go around criteria carefully.`,source_title:`UPDATED: Navy P-8A Poseidon Overshoots Hawaiian Runway, Splashes in Kaneohe Bay`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/2023/11/20/navy-p-8a-poseidon-overshoots-hawaiian-runway-splashes-in-kaneohe-bay-crew-safe`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m10`,date:`2023-09-17`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`F-35B`,family:`fighter`,place:`Williamsburg County, South Carolina (pilot ejected near Joint Base Charleston)`,lat:33.65,lon:-79.65,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`wx`,`sd`,`mx`,`populated`],phase:`approach`,fatal:!1,narrative:`While flying in heavy rain near Joint Base Charleston, a Marine F 35B pilot faced failures of both radios, the transponder, navigation aids and the helmet display and became disoriented. The pilot ejected, and the jet flew on by itself for more than 11 minutes before coming down in woods in Williamsburg County, where searchers took about 30 hours to find it. The Marine investigation found the pilot misjudged the situation as out of control flight and left a flyable aircraft, and no one on the ground was hurt.`,hazard:`In instrument weather with display or electrical failures, fall back on standby instruments and the autopilot and confirm the aircraft is truly uncontrollable before ejecting.`,source_title:`F-35 crash in South Carolina investigation`,source_url:`https://taskandpurpose.com/news/f-35-crash-south-carolina-investigation/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m11`,date:`2023-08-27`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`MV-22B`,family:`tiltrotor`,place:`Melville Island, Northern Territory, Australia`,lat:-11.6,lon:130.9,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`lz`],phase:`approach`,fatal:true,narrative:`During an exercise with Marine Rotational Force Darwin, an MV 22B from VMM 363 made three extreme right banks on final approach to its planned landing zone on Melville Island, stalled and could not recover, killing three Marines. The investigation found pilot error from a loss of situational awareness and no material or mechanical failure.`,hazard:`Stabilize the approach early and go around rather than correcting with steep banks close to the landing zone.`,source_title:`I MEF completes August 2023 MRF-D MV-22B Osprey mishap investigation`,source_url:`https://www.imef.marines.mil/Media/News/Press-Release-Article-Display/Article/3868543/i-mef-completes-august-2023-mrf-d-mv-22b-osprey-mishap-investigation`,source_kind:`press release`},
{id:`m12`,date:`2023-08-24`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`F/A-18D`,family:`fighter`,place:`Government land east of MCAS Miramar, San Diego, California`,lat:32.87,lon:-117.1,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`night`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Marine F/A 18D from a Beaufort based squadron crashed shortly before midnight on government property east of MCAS Miramar. The pilot, the only person aboard, was killed. The cause was under investigation at the time of reporting.`,hazard:`Night flights near base terrain demand disciplined instrument scan and altitude awareness, especially for crews operating away from their home field.`,source_title:`Marine Hornet pilot killed in crash near MCAS Miramar`,source_url:`https://taskandpurpose.com/news/marine-hornet-crash-miramar-california.md`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m13`,date:`2023-04-27`,service:`USA`,aircraft:`AH-64`,family:`helo_attack`,place:`Near Healy, Alaska`,lat:63.86,lon:-148.97,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`midair`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`Two AH 64 Apaches from the 1st Attack Battalion, 25th Aviation Regiment at Fort Wainwright collided and crashed near Healy, close to the entrance of Denali National Park, while returning from training. Three soldiers were killed and a fourth was injured.`,hazard:`When several aircraft fly together, brief spacing, lookout sectors and what each crew does if it loses sight of the aircraft ahead.`,source_title:`Three soldiers killed when two Army Apache helicopters crash in Alaska`,source_url:`https://stripes.com/theaters/us/2023-04-27/army-apache-helicopters-crash-alaska-9943558.html`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m14`,date:`2023-03-29`,service:`USA`,aircraft:`HH-60`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Trigg County, Kentucky, near Fort Campbell`,lat:36.83,lon:-87.72,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`midair`,`nvg`,`night`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`Two 101st Airborne Division HH 60 Black Hawks crashed during a night training exercise near Fort Campbell, killing all nine soldiers aboard. Army officials said the pilots were wearing night vision goggles, and the aircraft were flying at the time rather than conducting a medical evacuation drill.`,hazard:`Multiship night goggle training demands a firm plan for aircraft separation, lookout duties and lost visual contact procedures.`,source_title:`Flight data recorders found after deadly Black Hawk crash`,source_url:`https://www.armytimes.com/news/your-army/2023/04/05/flight-data-recorders-found-after-deadly-black-hawk-crash/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m15`,date:`2023-02-15`,service:`ARNG`,aircraft:`UH-60L`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Harvest, Alabama, north of Huntsville`,lat:34.84,lon:-86.71,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[],phase:`approach`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Tennessee Army National Guard UH 60 Black Hawk on a training flight crashed along Alabama Highway 53 in Harvest, Madison County, north of Huntsville. Both pilots aboard were killed.`,hazard:`Brief weather limits, instrument transition and inadvertent IMC procedures for local training flights, even short ones.`,source_title:`Black Hawk crash kills 2 Tennessee National Guard members (NBC News)`,source_url:`https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/black-hawk-helicopter-crash-kills-2-tennessee-national-guard-members-a-rcna70962`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m16`,date:`2022-08-16`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`T-45C`,family:`trainer`,place:`Naval Air Station Kingsville, Texas`,lat:27.51,lon:-97.81,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`bird`],phase:`approach`,fatal:!1,narrative:`A T 45C flown by an instructor pilot alone departed an outlying field and crashed on airfield property near the runway at NAS Kingsville after the pilot ejected. The investigation found a large bird was ingested into the engine and caused a loss of power, and it judged the mishap unavoidable with weather and maintenance not factors. It recommended wider use of avian radar and continued simulator training on bird strike engine failures.`,hazard:`Single engine jets have no backup after a bird ingestion, so check bird activity reports and brief engine failure actions for the departure and arrival paths.`,source_title:`Bird strike caused T-45 Goshawk crash last August, investigation finds`,source_url:`https://www.militarytimes.com/news/your-navy/2023/06/09/bird-strike-caused-t-45-goshawk-crash-last-august-investigation-finds/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m17`,date:`2022-06-08`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`MV-22B`,family:`tiltrotor`,place:`Training area near Glamis, California`,lat:32.99,lon:-115.07,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`mx`],phase:`training range`,fatal:true,narrative:`An MV 22B crashed in a remote training area near Glamis in Southern California, killing five Marines. The command investigation found a dual hard clutch engagement caused the engine and interconnect drive system to fail, leaving the right proprotor with no thrust and making controlled flight impossible.`,hazard:`Brief hard clutch engagement indications and procedures, and keep enough altitude in training profiles to manage a sudden drive system failure.`,source_title:`Clutch problem in Osprey led to death of 5 Marines in 2022, Corps says`,source_url:`https://www.militarytimes.com/news/your-marine-corps/2023/07/21/clutch-problem-in-osprey-led-to-death-of-5-marines-in-2022-corps-says/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m18`,date:`2022-03-23`,service:`ANG`,aircraft:`F-16CM`,family:`fighter`,place:`Beauregard Parish, Louisiana`,lat:30.65,lon:-93.35,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`civil_conflict`,`lowlevel`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:!1,narrative:`An Oklahoma Air National Guard F 16CM in a two ship alert training flight was told to make an unplanned intercept of a general aviation aircraft to read its tail number. Flying slow and low close to the civil aircraft, the pilot pressed an adjacent look alike switch instead of the flap switch, felt an unexpected shudder, believed the jet was out of control, and ejected with minor injuries. The board cited the mistaken ejection decision and poor flight leadership and discipline, including training rule violations.`,hazard:`Unbriefed intercepts of civil aircraft at low speed and altitude add risk, so stick to the briefed plan and confirm switch positions before acting on an unexpected aircraft response.`,source_title:`ACC releases Accident Investigation Board report for F-16CM crash in Louisiana`,source_url:`https://www.acc.af.mil/News/Article/3229388/acc-releases-accident-investigation-board-report-for-f-16cm-crash-in-louisiana/`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m19`,date:`2022-03-18`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`MV-22B`,family:`tiltrotor`,place:`Gratadalen valley near Bodo, Norway`,lat:66.95,lon:15.55,loc_precision:`approx 25 nm`,tags:[`terf`,`lowlevel`,`cfit`],phase:`low level`,fatal:true,narrative:`During Exercise Cold Response, a VMM 261 MV 22B left its authorized route and flew low altitude maneuvers in a mountain valley. It banked past its 60 degree limit to the left, then overcorrected beyond 80 degrees to the right, lost airspeed and altitude and could not recover, killing four Marines. Weather was clear and the investigation ruled it out as a factor.`,hazard:`Fly the authorized route and respect bank angle limits in confined valleys, where steep turns bleed energy and leave no room to recover.`,source_title:`2nd MAW releases command investigation into the MV-22B Osprey crash in Norway`,source_url:`https://www.2ndmaw.marines.mil/News/Article-View/Article/3127405/2nd-maw-releases-command-investigation-into-the-mv-22b-osprey-crash-in-norway-o/`,source_kind:`JAGMAN summary`},
{id:`m20`,date:`2022-02-22`,service:`ARNG`,aircraft:`UH-60`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Mineral Basin near Snowbird, Utah`,lat:40.565,lon:-111.64,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`dve`,`lz`,`form`,`terf`],phase:`landing`,fatal:!1,narrative:`Two Utah Army National Guard UH 60s were on mountain training when snow blown up during the first aircraft's landing likely cost its crew sight of the ground. Part of its rotor blade broke off and struck the second Black Hawk, which then landed quickly, and both aircraft were damaged with no injuries.`,hazard:`For snow landings, brief whiteout procedures, approach profile and spacing so trailing aircraft stay clear of the lead's snow cloud and rotor.`,source_title:`No injuries after 2 Black Hawk helicopters go down near Snowbird`,source_url:`https://www.ksl.com/article/50353784/no-injuries-after-2-black-hawk-helicopters-go-down-near-snowbird`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m21`,date:`2021-11-19`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`T-38C`,family:`trainer`,place:`Laughlin AFB, Texas`,lat:29.36,lon:-100.78,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`form`],phase:`landing`,fatal:true,narrative:`Two T 38Cs flew a formation approach in which one was supposed to land and the other to make a low approach, but miscommunication led both to land. The first jet ended up below the second where neither crew could see the other, and the second landed on top of it. A student pilot was killed and two instructors were injured; the board cited failure to state and confirm which jet would land, plus conflicting techniques and confusing call signs.`,hazard:`Before any split formation landing, state and confirm exactly which aircraft lands and which goes around, and abort if visual contact is lost.`,source_title:`19 NOV 21 T-38 Laughlin AIB Press Release`,source_url:`https://www.afjag.af.mil/Portals/77/AIB-Reports/2021/19NOV21%20T-38%20Laughlin%20Press%20Release.pdf`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m22`,date:`2021-09-19`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`T-45C`,family:`trainer`,place:`Lake Worth, Texas, near NAS JRB Fort Worth`,lat:32.81,lon:-97.44,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`bird`,`populated`],phase:`approach`,fatal:!1,narrative:`A T 45C on a training flight crashed in a Lake Worth neighborhood while on approach to Naval Air Station Joint Reserve Base Fort Worth, damaging three homes. Video shows a bird striking the jet before the pilot declared an emergency. Both pilots ejected and were hurt, the student after his parachute caught in power lines, and three people on the ground had minor injuries.`,hazard:`Approaches over neighborhoods near airfields carry bird strike risk at low altitude, so brief immediate actions for engine loss and where to point the aircraft before ejecting.`,source_title:`Pilots ejected from military training jet in Lake Worth (CBS Texas)`,source_url:`https://www.cbsnews.com/texas/news/power-lines-electrocute-pilots-ejected-from-military-training-jet`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m23`,date:`2021-08-31`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`MH-60S`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Aboard USS Abraham Lincoln, eastern Pacific off San Diego, California`,lat:32.3,lon:-118.2,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`ship`,`mx`],phase:`landing`,fatal:true,narrative:`Shortly after landing aboard USS Abraham Lincoln, an MH 60S suffered severe vibration and was lost, killing five aircrew. The Navy investigation found a damper hose had failed in flight, causing a complete loss of main rotor damping, and found no pilot or aircrew error.`,hazard:`Inspect main rotor damper hoses and fittings carefully and brief the response to abnormal vibration on deck, including when to shut down.`,source_title:`U.S. Navy Completes Investigation Into Fatal Helicopter Crash`,source_url:`https://www.navy.mil/Press-Office/Press-Releases/display-pressreleases/Article/3018680/us-navy-completes-investigation-into-fatal-helicopter-crash/`,source_kind:`press release`},
{id:`m24`,date:`2021-05-17`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`T-45C`,family:`trainer`,place:`Ricardo, near Naval Air Station Kingsville, Texas`,lat:27.42,lon:-97.85,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`midair`,`form`],phase:`formation`,fatal:!1,narrative:`Two T 45 trainers from a Kingsville training squadron collided in mid air about nine miles south of the air station. One jet landed safely at NAS Kingsville, while the instructor and student in the other ejected. All four pilots survived, and one was treated for minor injuries.`,hazard:`In formation training, brief lost sight and breakout procedures and keep clear lines of responsibility for separation between aircraft.`,source_title:`Two Navy T-45 Trainers Crash in Texas; All 4 Pilots Safe, 1 Treated for Minor Injuries`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/2021/05/17/two-navy-t-45-trainers-crash-in-texas-all-4-pilots-safe-1-treated-for-minor-injuries`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m25`,date:`2021-02-02`,service:`ARNG`,aircraft:`UH-60`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Near Lucky Peak, south of Boise, Idaho`,lat:43.53,lon:-116.06,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`iimc`,`wx`,`cfit`,`terf`,`night`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`An Idaho Army National Guard UH 60 on a routine evening training flight struck a mountainside near Lucky Peak, killing three aviators. Preliminary Guard findings said fog, mountain obscuration and precipitation took away the crew's visual references, and after transitioning to instruments the aircraft could not climb fast enough to clear rising terrain. Investigators found no mechanical failure.`,hazard:`In mountains with deteriorating weather, set firm turn back points and know the climb needed to clear terrain before visual references are lost.`,source_title:`Officials: Loss of visibility, sudden weather change contributed to Blackhawk crash`,source_url:`https://www.idahopress.com/eyeonboise/officials-loss-of-visibility-sudden-weather-change-contributed-to-blackhawk-crash/article_0ab831df-2751-559c-962c-794b2821ce28.html`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m26`,date:`2021-01-20`,service:`ARNG`,aircraft:`UH-60`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Mendon, New York, south of Rochester`,lat:42.99,lon:-77.5,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`night`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A New York Army National Guard UH 60 medical evacuation helicopter from the aviation support facility at Rochester crashed into a farm field in Mendon during an evening training flight around 6:30 p.m. All three Guard members aboard were killed.`,hazard:`Winter evening training flights bring early darkness and snow covered terrain, so brief illumination, weather and terrain cues before launch.`,source_title:`National Guard helicopter crash kills 3 in New York farmer's field`,source_url:`https://www.cbsnews.com/amp/news/national-guard-helicopter-crash-new-york-3-dead`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m27`,date:`2020-12-08`,service:`ANG`,aircraft:`F-16C`,family:`fighter`,place:`Hiawatha National Forest, Michigan`,lat:46.2,lon:-86.2,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`sd`,`night`,`nvg`,`wx`,`form`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Wisconsin Air National Guard F 16C was on a night alert training flight with a wingman when it lost GPS tracking shortly after takeoff. While the pilot troubleshot the navigation system the flight swapped leads, the jet entered weather, and visual contact with the wingman was lost; the aircraft then struck the ground and the pilot was killed without ejecting. The board found he did not recover from spatial disorientation, with weather, night vision goggle use, low light, and fixation on a minor system issue contributing.`,hazard:`At night in weather, fly the instruments first and set aside minor system troubleshooting until the aircraft is stable and clear of the formation.`,source_title:`ACC releases Accident Investigation Board Report for F-16 Crash in the Hiawatha`,source_url:`https://www.acc.af.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/2651324/acc-releases-accident-investigation-board-report-for-f-16-crash-in-the-hiawatha`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m28`,date:`2020-10-23`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`T-6B`,family:`trainer`,place:`Foley, Alabama`,lat:30.41,lon:-87.68,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`populated`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A T 6B trainer that took off from NAS Whiting Field on a routine training flight crashed in a residential area of Foley, Alabama, in the late afternoon. The instructor and the student pilot were killed. The Navy said no civilians were injured, though local reports said at least one house was damaged.`,hazard:`Training areas near coastal towns put houses under the flight path, so brief emergency landing options and keep maneuvering clear of populated areas.`,source_title:`UPDATED: Navy Identifies 2 Killed in Navy T-6B Texan II Trainer Crash in Alabama`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/2020/10/23/2-killed-in-navy-t-6b-texan-ii-trainer-crash-in-alabama`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m29`,date:`2020-09-29`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`F-35B`,family:`fighter`,place:`Near Ocotillo Wells, Imperial Valley, California`,lat:33.14,lon:-116.14,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`ar`,`midair`],phase:`refueling`,fatal:!1,narrative:`During aerial refueling in a Weapons and Tactics Instructor course in Southern California, an F 35B collided with a KC 130J tanker. The F 35B pilot ejected and the jet crashed near Ocotillo Wells, while the tanker crew, reporting two engines out, a fuel leak and only partial control, made an emergency landing near Thermal. All aircrew survived.`,hazard:`Brief tanker join up, closure limits and breakaway procedures, and know where the receiver and tanker will each go if contact is lost or a collision occurs.`,source_title:`Marines Release More Details on F-35B, KC-130J Collision`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/2020/10/01/marines-release-more-details-on-f-35b-kc-130j-collision`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m30`,date:`2020-06-30`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`F-16CM`,family:`fighter`,place:`Shaw AFB, South Carolina`,lat:33.97,lon:-80.47,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`night`,`ar`,`fuel`],phase:`landing`,fatal:true,narrative:`On a night training sortie, an F 16CM pilot could not complete aerial refueling and returned early for fuel. On final approach he misread the approach lighting, struck the localizer antenna short of the runway, and badly damaged the landing gear before going around. A cable arrestment was then attempted, the hook missed, and the pilot ejected but was killed after a series of ejection seat malfunctions.`,hazard:`At night, positively identify the runway threshold rather than the approach lights, and when the aircraft is damaged get expert input before choosing between an arrestment and a controlled ejection.`,source_title:`ACC releases Accident Investigation Board Report for F-16 Crash at Shaw AFB`,source_url:`https://www.acc.af.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/2409430/acc-releases-accident-investigation-board-report-for-f-16-crash-at-shaw-afb/`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m31`,date:`2020-05-19`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`F-35A`,family:`fighter`,place:`Eglin AFB, Florida`,lat:30.48,lon:-86.53,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`night`,`physio`],phase:`landing`,fatal:!1,narrative:`Returning from a night training mission, an F 35A touched down about 50 knots too fast on a shallow approach, bounced, and became airborne again. During the recovery the flight control logic opposed the pilot's inputs, and he ejected with serious injuries as the jet rolled and hit the runway. The board cited excess landing speed and a previously unknown flight control anomaly, with a misaligned helmet display, oxygen system fatigue, and simulator shortfalls contributing.`,hazard:`Fatigue at the end of a night sortie degrades crosscheck, so verify landing speed and glidepath against the numbers and go around early from any unstable approach.`,source_title:`Eglin F-35 Crash Blamed on Landing Speed, but Software, Helmet, Oxygen Also Faulted`,source_url:`https://www.airandspaceforces.com/eglin-f-35-crash-blamed-on-landing-speed-but-software-helmet-oxygen-also-faulted/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m32`,date:`2019-12-05`,service:`ARNG`,aircraft:`UH-60L`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Near Marty, southwest of St. Cloud, Minnesota`,lat:45.39,lon:-94.35,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`mx`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Minnesota Army National Guard UH 60L crashed in a field southwest of St. Cloud during a maintenance test flight, killing three Guard members. A Guard summary of the investigation said the number one engine failed during a maximum power check while the number two engine was at idle, because a hydromechanical unit had been installed without following the published procedure. It also found the crew did not respond to the emergency or carry out an autorotation.`,hazard:`Before engine checks on a test flight, brief the dual engine out risk, keep the idle engine ready, and rehearse the autorotation entry.`,source_title:`Mechanical failure, human error cited in Guard copter crash`,source_url:`https://foxbaltimore.com/news/nation-world/mechanical-failure-human-error-cited-in-guard-copter-crash`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m33`,date:`2019-11-21`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`T-38C`,family:`trainer`,place:`Vance AFB, Oklahoma`,lat:36.34,lon:-97.92,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`form`],phase:`landing`,fatal:true,narrative:`During a formation landing at Vance, a T 38C bounced after touchdown, rolled right, and skidded toward the other jet before lifting off and striking it with its landing gear. The aircraft crashed inverted and both pilots aboard were killed, while the crew of the other jet was unhurt. Investigators found the student made incorrect control inputs, starting aerodynamic braking too early, and the instructor did not take control in time.`,hazard:`In a formation landing, a bounce or drift toward the other aircraft calls for an immediate go around or instructor takeover rather than trying to salvage the landing.`,source_title:`Investigation into fatal Vance T-38 crash (Air & Space Forces Magazine)`,source_url:`https://airandspaceforces.com/?p=68917`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m34`,date:`2019-07-31`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`F/A-18E`,family:`fighter`,place:`Rainbow Canyon (Star Wars Canyon), Death Valley National Park, California`,lat:36.35,lon:-117.5,loc_precision:`range`,tags:[`lowlevel`,`terf`,`form`,`cfit`],phase:`low level`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Super Hornet leading a two ship low level training flight through Rainbow Canyon struck the canyon wall, killing the pilot, and debris injured seven tourists watching from the rim. The Navy command investigation found the jet was faster, lower and accelerating while descending as it approached a ridgeline higher than the one crossed the day before. It concluded the profile left too little time to react and called the likely cause a brief lapse in judgment, noting no evidence of showing off for spectators.`,hazard:`In canyon and terrain masking flight, control speed and descent before ridgelines, know the exact terrain ahead, and keep enough energy and room to exit if the turn goes wide.`,source_title:`Navy Concludes Experienced Pilot's 'Brief Lapse of Judgement' Root Cause of 'Star Wars' Canyon Crash`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/2020/05/28/navy-concludes-experienced-pilots-brief-lapse-of-judgement-root-cause-of-star-wars-canyon-crash`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m35`,date:`2019-05-01`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`T-6A`,family:`trainer`,place:`About 21 miles northeast of Sheppard AFB, Texas`,lat:34.2,lon:-98.25,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`sd`,`wx`],phase:`training range`,fatal:!1,narrative:`An instructor setting up a pilot instructor training sortie in a T 6A let the nose rise unnoticed at low airspeed and high power, and the aircraft departed controlled flight inverted. Once in the clouds the crew lost track of altitude, turn direction and rate of turn and did not apply the recovery checklist, so both pilots ejected with minor injuries. The board cited the instructor's fixation, the resulting stall, and failure to follow critical recovery steps.`,hazard:`Practice stalls and out of control maneuvers only in clear airspace with a firm recovery altitude, and know the recovery boldface by heart.`,source_title:`190501 AETC Sheppard AFB Texas T-6 AIB Media Release`,source_url:`https://media.defense.gov/2019/Dec/17/2002226083/-1/-1/0/190501-AETC-SHEPPARD%20AFB%20TEXAS-T-6%20AIB%20MEDIA%20RELEASE.PDF`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m36`,date:`2019-03-30`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`AH-1Z`,family:`helo_attack`,place:`Near Yuma, Arizona`,lat:32.69,lon:-114.63,loc_precision:`approx 25 nm`,tags:[`night`],phase:`training range`,fatal:true,narrative:`An AH 1Z Viper supporting the Weapons and Tactics Instructor course crashed at about 8:45 p.m. near Yuma, killing both pilots. The flight was part of an instructor pilot week used to refine procedures and test the training area. The cause was under investigation when it was reported.`,hazard:`Brief night range procedures, minimum altitudes and lighting conditions when flying unfamiliar or newly tested training areas.`,source_title:`Two Marines Killed in Arizona Helicopter Crash During Training Mission`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/2019/03/31/two-marines-killed-arizona-helicopter-crash-training-mission`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m37`,date:`2018-09-28`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`F-35B`,family:`fighter`,place:`Near Marine Corps Air Station Beaufort, South Carolina`,lat:32.48,lon:-80.72,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`mx`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:!1,narrative:`An F 35B from a Marine training squadron crashed near MCAS Beaufort, and the pilot ejected and survived with no one on the ground hurt. Initial data from the investigation led to a fleet wide inspection of a fuel tube in the F135 engine.`,hazard:`New type aircraft can carry undiscovered component defects, so treat engine caution indications seriously and brief engine failure and ejection options for the local area.`,source_title:`F-35s Grounded for Engine Inspections Following Crash Investigation Findings`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/2018/10/11/f-35s-grounded-engine-inspections-following-crash-investigation-findings`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m38`,date:`2018-05-02`,service:`ANG`,aircraft:`WC-130H`,family:`transport`,place:`Savannah/Hilton Head International Airport, Savannah, Georgia`,lat:32.13,lon:-81.2,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`mx`],phase:`takeoff`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Puerto Rico Air National Guard WC 130H on a ferry flight to the aircraft boneyard lost power on its number one engine during the takeoff roll, and the crew did not recognize the loss until just before liftoff. After becoming airborne the crew did not correctly apply engine failure procedures, a left rudder input led to a left wing stall, and the aircraft struck a state highway, killing all nine aboard. The board cited crew error, incomplete checklist execution, and a prior engine fault that maintenance had not properly fixed.`,hazard:`Brief engine failure on takeoff in detail, including abort criteria and rudder and turn direction away from the dead engine, especially when the aircraft has a known recent engine write up.`,source_title:`Puerto Rico Air National Guard WC-130 crash investigation results released`,source_url:`https://www.amc.af.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/1687750/puerto-rico-air-national-guard-wc-130-crash-investigation-results-released/`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m39`,date:`2018-04-04`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`F-16CM`,family:`fighter`,place:`Nevada Test and Training Range near Creech AFB, Nevada`,lat:36.6,lon:-115.67,loc_precision:`approx 25 nm`,tags:[`gloc`,`physio`],phase:`training range`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Thunderbirds F 16CM was practicing the team's high show demonstration on the Nevada range. After roughly 22 seconds of inverted flight around 5,500 feet above the ground, the pilot pulled into a descending half loop and lost consciousness from G forces. He did not regain awareness in time to recover or eject and was killed on impact.`,hazard:`Time spent inverted or at low G before a hard pull reduces G tolerance, so set up the anti G strain early and be ready to ease off the pull for any sign of tunnel vision.`,source_title:`F-16CM Thunderbird Accident Investigation Released`,source_url:`https://www.acc.af.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/1663212/f-16cm-thunderbird-accident-investigation-released/`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m40`,date:`2018-04-03`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`CH-53E`,family:`helo_heavy`,place:`LZ Paddles near El Centro, California`,lat:32.79,lon:-115.86,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`mx`,`lz`],phase:`landing`,fatal:true,narrative:`A CH 53E from the 3rd Marine Aircraft Wing crashed at a desert landing zone near El Centro, killing four Marines. The command investigation traced it to a defective part in a rotor servo, where a valve component broke down in hydraulic fluid and froze partly open, limiting the pilot's control.`,hazard:`Brief the symptoms of a flight control servo malfunction and the immediate actions for uncommanded or restricted control response near the ground.`,source_title:`Marines lay out cause of crash that killed four Marines in 2018`,source_url:`https://www.kpbs.org/news/2020/may/21/marines-layout-cause-crash-killed-four-marines-201/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m41`,date:`2018-03-14`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`F/A-18F`,family:`fighter`,place:`Off Naval Air Station Key West, Florida`,lat:24.575,lon:-81.69,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`water`],phase:`approach`,fatal:true,narrative:`An F/A 18F from NAS Oceana returning from a routine training mission crashed into shallow water off Key West while on approach to Naval Air Station Key West. A witness reported seeing a major malfunction, then the wings went vertical and there was a fireball. Both crew members died.`,hazard:`On approaches over water, brief immediate actions and ejection criteria for loss of control at low altitude, where recovery time is minimal.`,source_title:`Eyewitness report: F/A-18F exploded before fatal crash`,source_url:`https://www.marinecorpstimes.com/news/your-navy/2018/03/15/eyewitness-report-fa-18f-exploded-before-fatal-crash/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m42`,date:`2018-01-20`,service:`USA`,aircraft:`AH-64`,family:`helo_attack`,place:`National Training Center, Fort Irwin, California`,lat:35.26,lon:-116.68,loc_precision:`range`,tags:[],phase:`training range`,fatal:true,narrative:`An AH 64 Apache from the 4th Infantry Division at Fort Carson crashed during a routine training rotation at the National Training Center, killing both aviators.`,hazard:`Desert rotations combine unfamiliar terrain, dust and heavy tempo, so brief local hazards and crew rest before each training period.`,source_title:`Two soldiers killed in Apache crash`,source_url:`https://armytimes.com/news/your-army/2018/01/21/two-soldiers-killed-in-apache-crash`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m43`,date:`2017-10-01`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`T-45C`,family:`trainer`,place:`Cherokee National Forest near Tellico Plains, Tennessee`,lat:35.36,lon:-84.29,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`lowlevel`,`cfit`],phase:`low level`,fatal:true,narrative:`A T 45C from NAS Meridian carrying an instructor and a student crashed into wooded mountain terrain near Tellico Plains, killing both. The Navy report found the jet was flown below allowed altitudes and cited pilot error. It also described a culture in the training unit that let pilots fly outside the approved curriculum and leadership that did not ensure training followed approved publications.`,hazard:`Fly the approved profile and altitude floors in mountainous terrain, and treat any departure from the syllabus as an unbriefed and unacceptable risk.`,source_title:`Navy: Training jet flew too low before Tellico Plains crash`,source_url:`https://www.wdef.com/?p=73127`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m44`,date:`2017-09-06`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`A-10C`,family:`attack`,place:`Nevada Test and Training Range, about 55 miles northwest of Nellis AFB`,lat:36.8,lon:-115.75,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`midair`,`night`],phase:`training range`,fatal:!1,narrative:`Two A 10Cs from the Weapons School collided during a night close air support training mission on the Nevada range. One pilot had drifted about 1,400 feet above his assigned altitude block into the other jet's block, and both aircraft were destroyed while both pilots ejected with minor injuries. The board cited failure to follow altitude deconfliction, with task overload, a broken instrument scan, visual conditions, and reliance on an altitude alert he did not hear contributing.`,hazard:`In a busy night stack, altitude blocks are the only separation, so build regular altimeter checks into the scan and do not rely on an aural alert.`,source_title:`Pilot error caused two Air Force A-10s to collide in midair`,source_url:`https://www.militarytimes.com/news/2018/04/12/pilot-error-caused-two-air-force-a-10s-to-collide-in-midair/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m45`,date:`2017-08-15`,service:`USA`,aircraft:`UH-60`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Off Kaena Point, Oahu, Hawaii`,lat:21.58,lon:-158.3,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`night`,`water`,`form`],phase:`training range`,fatal:true,narrative:`An Army UH 60 Black Hawk from the 25th Combat Aviation Brigade went down in the ocean off Kaena Point, Oahu, during a night training flight with a second Black Hawk. All five soldiers aboard, two pilots and three crew members, were killed.`,hazard:`Night flight over open water offers few visual references, so brief altitude callouts, instrument cross checks and how a second aircraft keeps track of the first.`,source_title:`Army helicopter reported down off Hawaii (Army Times)`,source_url:`https://www.armytimes.com/news/your-army/2017/08/16/coast-guard-army-helicopter-reported-down-off-hawaii/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m46`,date:`2017-08-05`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`MV-22B`,family:`tiltrotor`,place:`Shoalwater Bay, off Queensland, Australia`,lat:-22.4,lon:150.5,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`ship`],phase:`landing`,fatal:true,narrative:`An MV 22B from VMM 265 attempting to land on the forward spot of USS Green Bay could not hold its hover, struck the ship and went into the sea, killing three Marines. The command investigation found the aircraft met excessive downwash recirculating off the hull, made worse by the forward spot, and noted it may have been carrying extra weight. Several passengers had missed egress training or were not wearing seatbelts.`,hazard:`Check power margin against actual weight before shipboard landings and brief downwash recirculation on forward spots, along with passenger egress and seatbelt checks.`,source_title:`Investigation: 2017 Osprey Crash Due to Heavy Downwash; Excessive Aircraft Weight May Have Contributed`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/?p=33742`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m47`,date:`2017-07-10`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`KC-130T`,family:`tanker`,place:`Near Itta Bena, Leflore County, Mississippi`,lat:33.49,lon:-90.32,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`mx`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Marine Reserve KC 130T that departed MCAS Cherry Point broke apart in flight and fell into a soybean field near Itta Bena, killing all 16 service members aboard. A JAGMAN investigation found a corroded propeller blade separated and struck the fuselage, starting a chain of failures. The corrosion had been missed and coated over during depot overhaul, and the report also cited squadron maintenance and oversight lapses.`,hazard:`Propeller and structural inspections are only as good as the process behind them, so crews should review maintenance history and report any propeller vibration or anomaly before flight.`,source_title:`Investigation: Corroded Propeller Blade Caused KC-130T Crash`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/2018/12/06/marine-corps-corroded-propeller-blade-that-broke-loose-caused-2017-kc-130t-crash`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m48`,date:`2017-04-17`,service:`USA`,aircraft:`UH-60`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Breton Bay Golf Course, Leonardtown, Maryland`,lat:38.28,lon:-76.65,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A UH 60 Black Hawk from the 12th Aviation Battalion at Davison Airfield, Fort Belvoir, crashed on the Breton Bay golf course in Leonardtown, Maryland, during a routine training exercise. One crew member was killed and two others were injured, one critically.`,hazard:`Training near populated areas calls for a brief on suitable forced landing areas along the route.`,source_title:`1 killed after Blackhawk crashes at Maryland golf course`,source_url:`https://www.fox6now.com/news/1-killed-after-blackhawk-crashes-at-maryland-golf-course`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m49`,date:`2016-12-13`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`MV-22B`,family:`tiltrotor`,place:`Reef off Abu, Nago, Okinawa, Japan`,lat:26.55,lon:128.06,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`ar`,`night`,`wx`],phase:`refueling`,fatal:!1,narrative:`During night aerial refueling training over the sea off Okinawa, an MV 22B's rotor blades struck the tanker's refueling line. With the aircraft shaking violently, the pilot chose not to fly over homes and set down in shallow water off Camp Schwab near Abu in Nago, and all five crew were rescued. A US military report summary attributed the mishap to pilot error during refueling in difficult weather.`,hazard:`Set clear weather and turbulence limits for night tanking and brief breakaway procedures and proprotor clearance from the drogue.`,source_title:`III MEF commander addresses MV-22 incident off the coast of Okinawa`,source_url:`https://www.marines.mil/News/Press-Releases/Press-Release-Display/Article/1029317/iii-mef-commander-addressed-mv-22-incident-off-the-coast-of-okinawa/`,source_kind:`press release`},
{id:`m50`,date:`2016-10-25`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`F/A-18C`,family:`fighter`,place:`Marine Corps Air Ground Combat Center, Twentynine Palms, California`,lat:34.29,lon:-116.16,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`night`],phase:`landing`,fatal:!1,narrative:`A Marine F/A 18C returning from a close air support exercise crashed on landing at Twentynine Palms at sunset after the pilot mistook a dirt section and a parallel taxiway for the runway and lost control on touchdown. The approach and runway lights had not been turned on, and flashing lights from nearby helicopters added to the confusion. The pilot ejected and survived, and the investigation cited the unlit airfield and the pilot's limited experience as the main factors.`,hazard:`At dusk arrivals to austere or lightly used fields, confirm runway lighting is on before the approach and verify the landing surface against known references.`,source_title:`F/A-18C Hornet crash result of below-average pilot's error and runway lighting`,source_url:`https://www.marinecorpstimes.com/news/your-marine-corps/2018/01/17/fa-18c-hornet-crash-result-of-below-average-pilots-error-and-runway-lighting/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m51`,date:`2016-08-18`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`HH-60G`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Nevada Test and Training Range near Nellis AFB, Nevada`,lat:37.0,lon:-115.8,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`night`,`form`,`lowlevel`],phase:`formation`,fatal:!1,narrative:`An HH 60G was trailing another helicopter at low altitude over mountainous terrain during a night tactical formation mission in a large exercise. As the flight paths converged, the gunner called for a break, and the copilot rolled into a 70 degree bank that the helicopter could not hold altitude through; it hit the ground and rolled. The crew had non life threatening injuries and the board cited the unintended convergence and the overbanked avoidance turn.`,hazard:`At night in mountainous terrain, terrain can funnel formation flight paths together, so brief lost visual and break turn limits that keep enough lift to hold altitude.`,source_title:`HH-60G accident investigation released`,source_url:`https://www.acc.af.mil/News/Article/1172989/hh-60g-accident-investigation-released`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m52`,date:`2016-06-02`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`F/A-18C`,family:`fighter`,place:`Smyrna Airport, Smyrna, Tennessee`,lat:35.99,lon:-86.52,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`lowlevel`,`wx`],phase:`training range`,fatal:true,narrative:`During a practice flight before an air show in Smyrna, Tennessee, a Blue Angels F/A 18C crashed while flying a split S maneuver, and the pilot was killed. The Navy JAGMAN investigation found the pilot began the maneuver about 300 feet too low and about 50 knots too fast with afterburners on. It named pilot error as the primary cause, with weather and fatigue as contributing factors and no material failure.`,hazard:`Before any descending maneuver, confirm entry airspeed, altitude and power setting against limits and brief a firm abort and recovery point.`,source_title:`Navy report: Blue Angels pilot flew too low, too fast (AVweb)`,source_url:`https://avweb.com/news/navy-report-blue-angels-pilot-flew-too-low-fast/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m53`,date:`2016-01-14`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`CH-53E`,family:`helo_heavy`,place:`Off Haleiwa, North Shore of Oahu, Hawaii`,lat:21.62,lon:-158.15,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`midair`,`form`,`night`],phase:`formation`,fatal:true,narrative:`Two CH 53E helicopters from Kaneohe Bay returning from a night training mission collided about 11 p.m. roughly two and a half miles off Oahu, killing all 12 Marines aboard. An official report found the trailing aircraft struck the lead and the pilots did not keep enough distance in the dark. It also found pilots had not met minimum flight hour goals and the squadron had neglected basic aviation practices.`,hazard:`Brief formation spacing, lost sight procedures and closure cues for low light nights over water, and weigh crew currency before flying formation in the dark.`,source_title:`Pilot error, poor training blamed in Hawaii dual helicopter collision that killed 12 Marines`,source_url:`https://cbsnews.com/news/hawaii-dual-helicopter-collision-12-marines-killed-pilot-error-poor-training`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m54`,date:`2015-11-23`,service:`USA`,aircraft:`UH-60`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Training Area 22, Fort Hood, Texas`,lat:31.2,lon:-97.75,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`lowlevel`],phase:`training range`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Black Hawk crewed by a First Army training brigade unit crashed in a remote training area at Fort Hood around sunset, killing four soldiers. The First Army 15 6 investigation found the pilot in command made a break turn that exceeded the maximum bank angle and stalled the aircraft, and it noted the unit was flying outside its training mission. The crew had not checked out of the area, so nearly two hours passed before the aircraft was known to be missing.`,hazard:`Brief maneuver limits for aggressive turns at low altitude, and keep flight following current so a missing aircraft is noticed quickly.`,source_title:`A year later, soldiers killed in crash remembered`,source_url:`https://kdhnews.com/military/a-year-later-soldiers-killed-in-crash-remembered/article_854d8a04-b12d-11e6-850a-870929e45e59.html`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m55`,date:`2015-07-07`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`F-16C`,family:`fighter`,place:`Near Moncks Corner, South Carolina`,lat:33.196,lon:-80.01,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`midair`,`civil_conflict`],phase:`approach`,fatal:true,narrative:`An F 16 from Shaw AFB, flying radar vectors from Charleston approach control for a practice instrument approach, collided near Moncks Corner with a Cessna 150 that had just departed Berkeley County Airport under visual flight rules and was not talking to air traffic control. Both people in the Cessna were killed and the F 16 pilot ejected with minor injuries. The NTSB found the approach controller did not provide an appropriate resolution to the conflict, with the limits of see and avoid as a contributing factor.`,hazard:`Radar vectors near a busy general aviation field do not guarantee separation from VFR traffic that is not talking to ATC, so keep an aggressive outside scan and act immediately on any traffic call.`,source_title:`NTSB Safety Recommendation Report: Educating Controllers on Two Midair Collisions (ASR1606)`,source_url:`https://www.ntsb.gov/investigations/AccidentReports/Reports/ASR1606.pdf`,source_kind:`NTSB`},
{id:`m56`,date:`2015-05-17`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`MV-22B`,family:`tiltrotor`,place:`Landing Zone Gull, Marine Corps Training Area Bellows, Oahu, Hawaii`,lat:21.36,lon:-157.71,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`dve`,`lz`,`mx`],phase:`landing`,fatal:true,narrative:`An MV 22B landing at LZ Gull at Bellows suffered a left engine compressor stall, lost power and hit hard, killing two Marines. The investigation found repeated, sustained hovering in brownout had built up sand and dust on the engine turbine, and it named pilot performance and an improper landing zone survey as the main contributing factors.`,hazard:`Survey dusty landing zones properly and minimize time hovering in brownout, since repeated dust ingestion can rob the engines of power.`,source_title:`Osprey mishap investigation completed (MARFORPAC)`,source_url:`https://www.marforpac.marines.mil/Media-Room/Press-Release/Article/631375/osprey-mishap-investigation-completed/`,source_kind:`press release`},
{id:`m57`,date:`2015-03-10`,service:`ARNG`,aircraft:`UH-60M`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Santa Rosa Sound near Hurlburt Field, Florida`,lat:30.4,lon:-86.69,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`sd`,`wx`,`iimc`,`water`,`night`,`lowlevel`],phase:`training range`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Louisiana Army National Guard UH 60M supporting joint training with Marine special operations crashed into Santa Rosa Sound as thick sea fog moved into the training area, killing four Guardsmen and seven Marines. The joint investigation found the direct cause was spatial disorientation of both pilots, who did not effectively shift from visual flight to instrument procedures as the fog arrived.`,hazard:`Over water at low altitude, brief the fog and visibility abort criteria and be ready to transition immediately to instruments when visual cues degrade.`,source_title:`Black Hawk crash investigation findings released`,source_url:`https://www.eglin.af.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/813958/black-hawk-crash-investigation-findings-released/`,source_kind:`press release`},
{id:`m58`,date:`2015-01-23`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`UH-1Y`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Marine Corps Air Ground Combat Center, Twentynine Palms, California`,lat:34.29,lon:-116.16,loc_precision:`range`,tags:[`mx`],phase:`training range`,fatal:true,narrative:`A UH 1Y from HMLA 169 crashed during a training exercise near Twentynine Palms, killing both pilots. An accident report released under the Freedom of Information Act found the main gearbox filter cover had been installed improperly, letting the transmission lose its oil in flight, and it also cited pilot misjudgment.`,hazard:`Verify recent maintenance on drive system components and brief the response to transmission oil pressure or temperature warnings, including landing as soon as possible.`,source_title:`Maintenance issues caused helo crash`,source_url:`https://www.marinecorpstimes.com/news/your-marine-corps/2015/10/25/investigation-faulty-filter-cover-pilot-error-caused-fatal-marine-helicopter-crash/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m59`,date:`2014-08-27`,service:`ANG`,aircraft:`F-15C`,family:`fighter`,place:`George Washington National Forest near Deerfield, Virginia`,lat:38.19,lon:-79.4,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`physio`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Massachusetts Air National Guard F 15C on a solo cross country flight to New Orleans began a steep descent from about 43,000 feet and the pilot declared an emergency moments later. The jet accelerated past supersonic speed and struck forested terrain inverted and steeply nose low with no ejection attempt, and the pilot was killed. The board found the pilot was incapacitated and unable to recover, but could not determine why.`,hazard:`On solo high altitude cruise, treat any cockpit environment or avionics cooling warning seriously, know oxygen and hypoxia procedures cold, and descend early while still clear headed.`,source_title:`AIB Report Executive Summary, F-15C T/N 86-0157, 27 August 2014`,source_url:`https://www.airandspaceforces.com/PDF/DRArchive/Documents/2015/July%202015/082714_F15C_VA.pdf`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m60`,date:`2014-01-08`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`MH-53E`,family:`helo_heavy`,place:`About 18 nm off Virginia Beach, Virginia`,lat:36.85,lon:-75.65,loc_precision:`approx 25 nm`,tags:[`mx`,`lowlevel`],phase:`low level`,fatal:true,narrative:`An MH 53E Sea Dragon towing a mine countermeasures device about 100 feet above the ocean caught fire and crashed off Virginia Beach, killing three of the five aboard. The JAG investigation found electrical wiring had chafed against a fuel transfer tube, likely allowing an arc to breach the tube and ignite fuel, and thick smoke filled the cockpit so the pilots could not see.`,hazard:`Brief smoke and fire procedures for low altitude flight over water, and look closely at wire bundles routed near fuel lines during preflight.`,source_title:`Investigation: Sea Dragon Crash Result of Mechanical Fault`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/2014/09/11/investigation-sea-dragon-crash-result-mechanical-fault`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m61`,date:`2013-03-11`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`EA-6B`,family:`attack`,place:`Near Harrington, eastern Washington`,lat:47.48,lon:-118.25,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`mtr`,`lowlevel`,`cfit`],phase:`low level`,fatal:true,narrative:`An EA 6B Prowler from NAS Whidbey Island crashed in rural eastern Washington while flying the VR 1355 low level training route, killing all three crew members. A JAGMAN investigation attributed the crash to controlled flight into terrain, finding the crew was slow to recognize the closing ground and that an aggressive pull on the controls caused an accelerated stall. It also noted the relative inexperience of both pilots.`,hazard:`On low level routes, set and brief hard altitude floors and recovery cues early, and avoid abrupt pull ups near stall margins when terrain closure is recognized late.`,source_title:`2013 Prowler Crash That Killed Three Found to Be Result of 'Pilot Error'`,source_url:`https://news.usni.org/2014/03/12/2013-prowler-crash-killed-three-found-result-pilot-error`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m62`,date:`2012-07-01`,service:`ANG`,aircraft:`C-130H3 (MAFFS)`,family:`transport`,place:`White Draw Fire near Edgemont, South Dakota`,lat:43.3,lon:-103.83,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`wx`,`lowlevel`],phase:`low level`,fatal:true,narrative:`A North Carolina Air National Guard C 130 fitted with a modular airborne firefighting system was making a retardant drop on a South Dakota wildfire when it flew into a thunderstorm microburst. Despite full power the crew could not regain airspeed and the aircraft struck a plateau, killing four crew while two loadmasters survived. The board found several factors contributed, including the crew's decision to continue the drop near the storm, the lead aircraft's inadequate storm warning, and conflicting storm avoidance guidance.`,hazard:`Thunderstorm outflow near a low level drop or route can produce downdrafts that exceed aircraft performance, so set clear storm distance limits and let any crew member call a knock it off.`,source_title:`Crew decision to fly in severe weather contributed to fatal C-130 crash, report finds`,source_url:`https://www.stripes.com/news/2012-11-14/crew-decision-to-fly-in-severe-weather-contributed-to-fatal-c-130-crash-report-finds-1873407.html`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m63`,date:`2012-06-13`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`CV-22B`,family:`tiltrotor`,place:`Eglin Range north of Navarre, Florida`,lat:30.47,lon:-86.86,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`form`],phase:`formation`,fatal:!1,narrative:`A CV 22B from Hurlburt Field was flying in a two ship formation on a routine evening training mission over the Eglin Range when it rolled left without command, lost altitude quickly, and hit the ground. All five crew were injured, none fatally, and the aircraft was destroyed. The board found the crew did not keep the aircraft clear of the lead aircraft's wake.`,hazard:`Tiltrotor rotor wash and wake extend well behind and below the lead, so brief formation spacing and positions that keep the trail aircraft out of it.`,source_title:`CV-22 Accident Investigation Board Complete (AFSOC)`,source_url:`https://www.globalsecurity.org/military/library/news/2012/08/mil-120830-afsoc01.htm`,source_kind:`press release`},
{id:`m64`,date:`2012-04-06`,service:`USN`,aircraft:`F/A-18D`,family:`fighter`,place:`Mayfair Mews apartments, Virginia Beach, Virginia`,lat:36.83,lon:-76.05,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`mx`,`populated`],phase:`takeoff`,fatal:!1,narrative:`After taking off from a nearby base for a routine training mission over the Atlantic, a Navy F/A 18D suffered failure of both engines from two unrelated problems and crashed into an apartment complex in Virginia Beach. Both crew members ejected at low altitude and survived, seven people were injured, and 27 apartments were destroyed. The Navy investigation found the right engine ingested a flammable liquid that caused a compressor failure while the left afterburner failed to light, and it did not attribute the crash to human error.`,hazard:`Departures over dense housing leave little room for a dual engine loss, so brief ejection decision altitudes and the clearest available impact area on the departure path.`,source_title:`Rare engine malfunction caused Virginia Navy jet crash`,source_url:`https://www.cbsnews.com/news/rare-engine-malfunction-caused-virginia-navy-jet-crash/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m65`,date:`2012-02-22`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`AH-1W / UH-1Y`,family:`helo_attack`,place:`Yuma Training Range Complex near the Chocolate Mountains, southeastern California`,lat:33.2,lon:-115.3,loc_precision:`range`,tags:[`midair`,`night`],phase:`training range`,fatal:true,narrative:`An AH 1W Cobra and a UH 1Y Huey from the 3rd Marine Aircraft Wing collided in flight at about 8 p.m. during a night training exercise on a remote part of the Yuma range complex. All seven Marines aboard the two aircraft were killed while preparing to deploy.`,hazard:`Brief deconfliction plans, altitude blocks and lighting for multiple aircraft working the same range at night.`,source_title:`Yuma crash investigation, Camp Pendleton Marines`,source_url:`https://patch.com/california/oceanside-camppendleton/yuma-crash-investigation-marines-camp-pendleton`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m66`,date:`2011-03-29`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`CH-53D`,family:`helo_heavy`,place:`Kaneohe Bay, Oahu, Hawaii`,lat:21.46,lon:-157.8,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`night`,`mx`],phase:`approach`,fatal:true,narrative:`A CH 53D on a night training flight came down hard on a sandbar in Kaneohe Bay about two miles from the air station, killing one crew member and injuring the other three. A portion of the official investigation attributed the mishap to a catastrophic mechanical failure, and the wing commander praised the crew's actions.`,hazard:`Brief immediate actions and ditching or forced landing options over water near the field at night, when shoreline and sandbars are hard to judge.`,source_title:`Honolulu Star-Advertiser report on Kaneohe Bay CH-53D investigation`,source_url:`https://staradvertiser.com/?p=290963`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m67`,date:`2010-11-16`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`F-22A`,family:`fighter`,place:`Northeast of Cantwell, Alaska`,lat:63.5,lon:-148.6,loc_precision:`approx 25 nm`,tags:[`sd`,`physio`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`An F 22 on a training mission in interior Alaska suffered a malfunction that cut off the pilot's oxygen supply. The pilot spent about 50 seconds trying to restore oxygen flow without activating the backup oxygen system, and the jet dove into the ground. The Air Force board blamed the pilot's failure to start a timely dive recovery, citing channelized attention and unrecognized spatial disorientation, but the DoD Inspector General later said that conclusion was not supported by the facts.`,hazard:`When an oxygen or life support warning appears, fly the jet first, keep the instrument scan going, and go straight to emergency oxygen and a descent rather than troubleshooting.`,source_title:`Pentagon IG disputes Air Force probe of F-22 crash in Alaska (Stars and Stripes)`,source_url:`https://www.stripes.com/news/us/pentagon-ig-disputes-air-force-probe-of-f-22-crash-in-alaska-1.207503`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m68`,date:`2010-07-28`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`C-17A`,family:`transport`,place:`Joint Base Elmendorf Richardson, Alaska`,lat:61.25,lon:-149.8,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`lowlevel`],phase:`takeoff`,fatal:true,narrative:`A C 17 practicing a demonstration routine for a local air show stalled shortly after takeoff and crashed on the base, killing all four crew and damaging part of the Alaska Railroad. The board found the pilot flew aggressively outside established parameters and the aircraft's limits and did not take stall recovery actions. Other crew members did not recognize or speak up about the developing danger.`,hazard:`Low altitude demonstration maneuvering leaves no room to recover from a stall, so fly only the approved profile and have every crew member call out bank, speed, and stall warnings without hesitation.`,source_title:`Air Force releases findings on Alaska C-17 fatal mishap`,source_url:`https://www.pacaf.af.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/594582/air-force-releases-findings-on-alaska-c-17-fatal-mishap/`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m69`,date:`2009-05-05`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`AH-1W`,family:`helo_attack`,place:`Cleveland National Forest near Kitchen Creek Road and Interstate 8, California`,lat:32.73,lon:-116.45,loc_precision:`area`,tags:[`night`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`An AH 1W Super Cobra from the 3rd Marine Aircraft Wing crashed at about midnight in the Cleveland National Forest north of Interstate 8. Both pilots were killed. The Marine Corps release reporting the crash did not state a cause.`,hazard:`Brief night terrain clearance and minimum altitudes for the mountains east of San Diego, where dark, sparsely lit terrain gives few visual cues.`,source_title:`Super Cobra crashes in national forest`,source_url:`https://www.hqmc.marines.mil/News/Article/Article/552832/super-cobra-crashes-in-national-forest/`,source_kind:`press release`},
{id:`m70`,date:`2008-12-08`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`F/A-18D`,family:`fighter`,place:`University City, San Diego, California`,lat:32.866,lon:-117.218,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`mx`,`populated`],phase:`approach`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Marine F/A 18D on a training flight from an aircraft carrier lost its right engine to an oil leak shortly after takeoff, then lost the second engine to a fuel delivery problem while trying to reach MCAS Miramar instead of the closer NAS North Island. The pilot ejected, and the jet struck homes in University City, killing four people on the ground. The Marine investigation described a complex emergency made worse by a series of well intentioned but incorrect decisions in the cockpit and the squadron ready room.`,hazard:`With a single engine emergency, brief the nearest suitable field and an approach path that avoids populated areas before choosing a preferred home base.`,source_title:`US military blames San Diego jet crash on bad decisions`,source_url:`https://www.theregister.com/2009/03/04/san_diego_crash_verdict/`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m71`,date:`2004-11-29`,service:`USA`,aircraft:`UH-60`,family:`helo_utility`,place:`Near Bruceville Eddy, McLennan County, Texas`,lat:31.31,lon:-97.25,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`wire`,`wx`,`iimc`,`cfit`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:true,narrative:`A Fort Hood UH 60 traveling to Red River Army Depot flew in thick morning fog into the support wires of a television transmission tower roughly 1,800 feet tall and crashed, killing all seven aboard. The tower's warning lights had failed after storms the week before.`,hazard:`In low visibility, know every tall tower and guy wire field on the route and do not count on obstruction lighting being in service.`,source_title:`Army helicopter crashes; all 7 aboard die`,source_url:`https://www.nbcnews.com/id/wbna6607774`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m72`,date:`2004-08-13`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`CH-53D`,family:`helo_heavy`,place:`Okinawa International University, Ginowan, Okinawa, Japan`,lat:26.276,lon:127.756,loc_precision:`town`,tags:[`mx`],phase:`cruise`,fatal:!1,narrative:`A CH 53D from Futenma lost tail rotor control and crashed onto a university campus next to the air station, injuring all three crew members but no civilians. The Marine command investigation found a cotter pin had not been reinstalled on a tail rotor flight control bolt after an adjustment, so the bolt worked loose. It cited confusion on the flight line about the type of rigging being done and maintainer fatigue from very long workdays.`,hazard:`After any flight control maintenance, confirm the work and hardware were fully inspected, and treat a fatigued maintenance crew as a risk to the aircraft you are about to fly.`,source_title:`Copter incident report cites confusion, fatigue on Futenma flight line`,source_url:`https://www.stripes.com/news/2004-11-13/copter-incident-report-cites-confusion-fatigue-on-futenma-flight-line-1961036.html`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m73`,date:`2003-06-13`,service:`USAF`,aircraft:`F-16`,family:`fighter`,place:`Gila Bend Auxiliary Airfield, Arizona`,lat:32.89,lon:-112.72,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`bird`,`form`],phase:`takeoff`,fatal:!1,narrative:`The lead of a four ship F 16 formation on a low level training mission saw a dark blur pass under the nose just after departing Gila Bend and immediately lost thrust after the engine ingested a turkey vulture. Unable to get back to the field, the pilot turned away from airfield buildings and ejected, and the jet crashed in open desert. He was examined and released.`,hazard:`Large soaring birds are common at low altitude over desert fields in summer, so check bird hazard conditions and plan a flameout or ejection option on departure.`,source_title:`Officials release F-16 accident report`,source_url:`https://www.af.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/138393/officials-release-f-16-accident-report`,source_kind:`AIB summary`},
{id:`m74`,date:`2000-12-11`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`MV-22B`,family:`tiltrotor`,place:`Near MCAS New River, Jacksonville, North Carolina`,lat:34.71,lon:-77.44,loc_precision:`approx 10 nm`,tags:[`night`,`mx`],phase:`approach`,fatal:true,narrative:`During a night training flight, an MV 22B crashed about seven miles from its home field at New River. The completed investigation found a chafed hydraulic line ruptured, and the flight control software then prompted repeated resets that produced erratic pitch, roll and yaw until the aircraft stalled. The crew was found to have responded correctly, and four Marines were killed.`,hazard:`Brief how the flight control system responds to hydraulic failures and which resets or switch actions can make a degraded aircraft worse.`,source_title:`Corps cites software failure in Osprey crash (via FAS)`,source_url:`https://man.fas.org/dod-101/sys/ac/docs/man-ac-v22-010407.htm`,source_kind:`news`},
{id:`m75`,date:`2000-04-08`,service:`USMC`,aircraft:`MV-22B`,family:`tiltrotor`,place:`Marana Regional Airport, near Tucson, Arizona`,lat:32.409,lon:-111.218,loc_precision:`base`,tags:[`night`,`form`],phase:`approach`,fatal:true,narrative:`An MV 22B flying a night training mission from MCAS Yuma descended too fast at low airspeed while trying to join behind its lead in line abreast formation on approach to Marana, and entered vortex ring state. Marine officials said the descent rate was about 250 percent of the acceptable rate, and that an unexpected tailwind and deviations from the flight plan left both aircraft well above the planned altitude. All 19 Marines aboard were killed.`,hazard:`Brief descent rate limits at low airspeed, and plan the approach so a late, high arrival is a go around rather than a steep catch up descent in formation.`,source_title:`Marine Officials Blame Human Factors in Osprey Crash (American Forces Press Service, via FAS)`,source_url:`https://man.fas.org/dod-101/sys/ac/docs/man-ac-v22-000728.htm`,source_kind:`press release`}
];
